*******************************************************************************************                                                                                        **		Apple IIgs Printer Driver                                                        **                                                                                        **		File: imager.aii -- Low Level Driver: Pixmap > ESC Codes > Communications        **                                                                                        **		Written by Ben Koning                                                            **		Copyright (C) 1990 Apple Computer, Inc.                                          **                                                                                        *******************************************************************************************							include		'equates.aii'																												include		'm16.util'							include		'm16.intmath'							include		'm16.event'							include		'm16.misctool'							include		'e16.quickdraw'ImagerProc					proc		export**IMAGER: LOW-LEVEL PRINTER DRIVER ROUTINES**These routines are the only ones which communicate with the printer device.  They are*capable of providing paper motion control and a process of marking the paper with the*image of a bitmap supplied by the caller, in various resolutions (that is, various*sizes).  It is the intention that the caller request that the imager mark the page in*a high resolution with a large bitmap, the latter compensating for the former so that*the resulting image appears at the correct size, but with increased resolution.**This particular imager is feature-reduced and does not support color.  In fact, it*does not support grayscale very well either.  Instead, it is optimized for speed*performance by means of white space skipping, direct source pixel to printer pixel*conversion, and data compression.**The following entry points are supported:**	ImagerOpen				Establishes unique connection to printer*	ImagerClose				Releases unique connection to printer*	ImagerSetPaperType		Sets up physical paper type*	ImagerSetLocInfo		Sets up locinfo struct of bitmap and sets up our color map table*	ImagerSetResolution		Sets up dpi-quality (size of each printer pixel)*	ImagerSetVCondense		Sets up double or single vertical stretching*	ImagerSetIdleProc		Sets up idle proc to be called periodically*	ImagerSetAbortPoll		Sets up address to listen for to cause abort*	ImagerGetVAlignFactor	Returns vertical size to which bitmap must be aligned*	ImagerGetDeviceID		Confirms identity of printer*	ImagerReset				Resets printer mechanics to default values*	ImagerFormfeed			Outputs a form feed character*	ImagerLinefeed			Moves the paper down by a specified distance*	ImagerPrint				Images, compresses, and sends a graphics bitmap**The imager, like other modules of the print driver, uses "ParamXXXXY" direct*page variables defined in the equates module.**Entry points that require pointers should be called with the low word in X*and the high word in Y.  Entry points that require input values should be*called with the A register set.  Output, if any, is given in the A register*and carry flag.**If something other than NIL is passed for the IdleProc, that location will*be JSL-ed to with our environment saved.  The Command-Period printing*interrupt request from the user is checked for even if an IdleProcPtr is*given (Command-Period causes the imager to abort and return $80 status).*The address given in ImagerSetAbortPoll is checked after the idleproc is*executed; this allows a high-level driver to allow the idleproc to set*a global variable such as PrSetError.**The coordinates given in ImagerSetLocInfo must be such that Y1<Y2 and*X1<X2.  The X coordinates should be byte-aligned.  Mixed 640-and-320*modes within the same bitmap is not supported.  This call initializes*values used during printing, such as the color pixel conversion table*which maps screen pixels into printer pixels.**Within the chunky color pixels of the bitmap, the color table entries for*%00 or %0000 are assumed to be pure black and those for %11 or %1111 are*assumed to be pure white.  A pure black and a pure white should always*exist in the standard color table entries.  If this is not the case, then*those pixels in the bitmap which refer to %00/%0000 or %11/%1111 will be*incorrectly printed black or white, respectively.  Also, if there are*pure black/white colors, but assigned to nonstandard locations in the*color table, then printing may also be incorrect.**Notes on terminology: In these routines, "band" refers to one scan of the*print head.  Do not confuse this with the printing bands into which the*high-level driver print loop routines split up each page due to possible*memory constraints.  Also, note the distinctions made in the comments*between "source" and "printer" pixels.  "Source" pixels are the input to*the imager (and are in fact usually in an off-screen buffer), and "printer"*pixels are the dots which are sent to the printer device.***IMAGEROPEN: Establishes unique connection with printer and initializes the imager:*							export ImagerOpenImagerOpen							stz AbortFlag						;zero our abort flag							stz Resolution						;default 75 dpi							stz PaperType						;default USLetter paper type							stz VerticalCondenseFlag			;default no vertical condense							stz IdleProcPtr+0					;default no idle procedure							stz IdleProcPtr+2							stz AbortPollPtr+0					;default no abort poll location							stz AbortPollPtr+2														pushlong #0							;ask port driver to open connection							pushlong #0							ldx #$1C13							;_PrDevOpen							jsl $E10000							rts**IMAGERCLOSE: Releases unique connection with printer and terminates the imager:*							export ImagerCloseImagerClose							ldx #$1F13							;_PrDevClose							jsl $E10000							rts**IMAGERGETVALIGNFACTOR: Returns vert align needed for some printers with band print models -> ACC:*							export ImagerGetVAlignFactorImagerGetVAlignFactor							lda #ImagerQDPattVAlignFactor		;any-vertical-size bitmap is ok, but							rts									;allow for quickdraw patterns**IMAGERGETDEVICEID: Finds out if we're connected to correct device.  A/carry set if correct device:*							export ImagerGetDeviceIDImagerGetDeviceID							lda #1								;always return true; we could not							sec									;obtain a reliable response and it							rts									;is not documented**IMAGERSETPAPERTYPE: Informs imager of physical paper type to set during reset.  Pass type -> ACC:**The types supported by the printer are: 0=USLetter, 1=USLegal, 2=A4Letter, 3=#10Envelope*							export ImagerSetPaperTypeImagerSetPaperType							and #%11							;do rudamentary range clip for 0..3							sta PaperType						;set our global variable							rts**IMAGERSETLOCINFO: Informs us of bitmap dims with locinfo/inits color map table.  Ptr lo->X, hi->Y:*							export ImagerSetLocInfoImagerSetLocInfo							stx ParamLongA+0					;access caller's locinfo struct							sty ParamLongA+2							ldy #oportSCB						;obtain the current graphics mode							lda [ParamLongA],y					;and store as $00/$80 in static var							and #$0080							sta SourceMode														ldy #optrToPixImage					;obtain pointer to caller's bitmap							lda [ParamLongA],y					;and store in our static variable							sta SourcePixPtr+0							iny							iny							lda [ParamLongA],y							sta SourcePixPtr+2														ldy #owidth							;obtain byte-width and store							lda [ParamLongA],y							sta SourceByteWidth														ldy #oboundsRect+ov1				;store beginning and ending raster							lda [ParamLongA],y					;lines of the source bitmap; note							sta SourceYLineBegin				;that Y1 must be smaller than Y2							ldy #oboundsRect+ov2							lda [ParamLongA],y							sta SourceYLineEnd														ldy #oboundsRect+oh1				;convert beginning X coordinate to							lda [ParamLongA],y					;byte offset and store							lsr a							ldx SourceMode						;320: 2 pix/byte, 640: 4 pix/byte							beq SeLoDivX1Its320SeLoDivX1Its640				lsr aSeLoDivX1Its320				sta SourceXByteBegin							ldy #oboundsRect+oh2				;convert ending X coordinate to							lda [ParamLongA],y					;byte offset and store							lsr a							ldx SourceMode						;320: 2 pix/byte, 640: 4 pix/byte							beq SeLoDivX2Its320SeLoDivX2Its640				lsr aSeLoDivX2Its320				sta SourceXByteEnd							brl BuildPixConvertTable			;build default pix cvt table; exit**IMAGERSETRESOLUTION: Sets size of each printer pixel to 75/150/300 dpi.  Pass 0/1/2 -> ACC:*							export ImagerSetResolutionImagerSetResolution							and #%11							;do rudamentary range clip							sta Resolution						;store it in global static var							rts**IMAGERSETVCONDENSE: Sets up 2x/1x-vert-size to compensate for GS fonts.  Pass 0/1: no/yes -> ACC:*							export ImagerSetVCondenseImagerSetVCondense							and #%1								;make sure it's only 0 or 1							sta VerticalCondenseFlag			;store it in global static var							rts**IMAGERSETIDLEPROC: Sets proc to be called during printing.  Pass ptr or NIL lo->X, hi->Y:*							export ImagerSetIdleProcImagerSetIdleProc							stx IdleProcPtr+0							sty IdleProcPtr+2							rts**IMAGERSETABORTPOLL: Sets adrs; if goes non-0 during print, we abort.  Pass ptr/NIL lo->X, hi->Y:*							export ImagerSetAbortPollImagerSetAbortPoll							stx AbortPollPtr+0							sty AbortPollPtr+2							rts**IMAGERRESET: Resets the printer logic and mechanics to default or printer-control-panel settings:*							export ImagerResetImagerReset							lda #ImReResetCommand				;main printer reset command							jsr WriteShort														ldx PaperType						;setup values for paper type command							bne ImRe1							;based on PaperType == 0,1,2,3ImReItsLtr					lda	#ImRePaperTypeCommandLtr							bra ImReDoPaperTypeImRe1						dex							bne ImRe2ImReItsLgl					lda #ImRePaperTypeCommandLgl							bra ImReDoPaperTypeImRe2						dex							bne ImReItsEnvImReItsA4					lda #ImRePaperTypeCommandA4							bra ImReDoPaperTypeImReItsEnv					lda #ImRePaperTypeCommandEnvImReDoPaperType				jsr WriteShort						;paper size command							lda #ImRePerfSkipCommandOff			;vertical perforation skip command							jsr WriteShort							lda #ImRePaperFeedCommandTray		;arrange to feed envelope if necc							ldx PaperType							cpx #3							bne ImReDoPaperFeed							lda #ImRePaperFeedCommandEnvImReDoPaperFeed				jsr WriteShort						;paper feed source command							rts							ImReResetCommand			dc.b 2							dc.b $1B,$45							ImRePaperTypeCommandLtr		dc.b 5							dc.b $1B,$26,$6C,$32,$41							ImRePaperTypeCommandLgl		dc.b 5							dc.b $1B,$26,$6C,$33,$41							ImRePaperTypeCommandA4		dc.b 6							dc.b $1B,$26,$6C,$32,$36,$41							ImRePaperTypeCommandEnv		dc.b 6							dc.b $1B,$26,$6C,$38,$31,$41							ImRePerfSkipCommandOff		dc.b 5							dc.b $1B,$26,$6C,$30,$4CImRePaperFeedCommandTray	dc.b 5							dc.b $1B,$26,$6C,$31,$48							ImRePaperFeedCommandEnv		dc.b 5							dc.b $1B,$26,$6C,$33,$48**IMAGERFORMFEED: Causes the printer to eject the current page:*							export ImagerFormfeedImagerFormfeed							lda #ImFfFormfeedCommand							brl WriteShortImFfFormfeedCommand			dc.b 5							dc.b $1B,$26,$6C,$30,$48**IMAGERLINEFEED: Moves the paper down by a specified distance.  Pass distance in 1/72ths -> ACC:*							export ImagerLinefeedImagerLinefeed							sta ParamWordA						;multiply by 10 to get 1/720ths...							asl a								;*2							asl a								;*4							asl a								;*8							clc							adc ParamWordA						;*9							clc							adc ParamWordA						;*10							pha									;pass number of 1/720ths							pushlong #ImLfLineFeedCommandNum	;pass where to put ascii number							pushword #4							;ascii number space is 4 digits long							pushword #0							;the number is unsigned							_Int2Dec							;convert and store into command str							lda #ImLfLineFeedCommand			;output command string and exit							brl WriteShort							ImLfLineFeedCommand			dc.b 9								;command to move current print							dc.b $1B,$26,$61,$2B				;position down by number ofImLfLineFeedCommandNum		dc.b 'XXXX'							;1/720th inches							dc.b $56**IMAGERPRINT: Converts/compresses/sends bitmap referred by locinfo.  ACC/c -> Abort status:**This routine converts the bitmap that has been previously specified with the set-locinfo call*into printer-ready pixels and causes it to be printed.  In doing so, we employ a fast white*scanner and utilize the pixel conversion table that was set up with the BuildPixConverTable*routine.  CompressSend is called each time after the printer-pix-buffer has been filled by the*completed processing of the current raster line.  After many CompressSend calls, we also*periodically call IdleProcAbortCheck and terminate the imaging process if necessary.**Variables used within the scope of doing all lines:*	ParamLongD has pointer to beginning of current source line; it is inc by source width*	ParamWordE has count of number of source lines that have been processed so far**Variables within the scope of each line:*	Y register has index into next byte position of source-pixel-buffer from ParamLongD*	ParamWordF has index into next available byte of printer-pixel-buffer*							export ImagerPrintImagerPrint*Send printer commands to initiate the proper graphics modes:							ldx Resolution						;send command to select one of the							beq ImPr_res75						;resolution modes; the higher the							dex									;resolution, the smaller the pr pix							beq ImPr_res150ImPr_res300					lda	#ImPrGraphics300DPICommand							bra ImPr_res_setImPr_res150					lda #ImPrGraphics150DPICommand							bra ImPr_res_setImPr_res75					lda #ImPrGraphics75DPICommandImPr_res_set				jsr WriteShort							lda #ImPrGraphicsStartCommand		;send start-of-graphics command							jsr WriteShort														lda #ImPrGraphicsCompactCommand		;send select-compact-mode command							jsr WriteShort*Initialize vertical loop counters:							pha									;setup plD with address of starting							pha									;source raster line by doing							pushword SourceYLineBegin			;(y1 * raster_width) + pix_map_base							pushword SourceByteWidth							_Multiply							clc									;prepare to add							pla									;get lo word of multiply result							adc SourcePixPtr+0					;add to pix map base and store lo							sta ParamLongD+0							pla									;get hi word of multiply result							adc SourcePixPtr+2					;add to pix map base and store hi							sta ParamLongD+2														lda SourceYLineBegin				;reset vertical line counter in pwE							sta ParamWordE*Head of vertical loop for doing all raster lines:ImPr_vertical_loop*Init for converting one horizontal source-pixel line into a printer-pixel line:							stz ParamWordF						;reset print-pix-buffer index in pwF							jsr ClearPrintPixBuffer				;zero the print-pix-buffer itself							lda SourceXByteEnd					;reset end-of-source-line terminator							sta ImPr_white_eoln+1				;in the white-elimination loop							ldy SourceXByteBegin				;reset source-pix-line index in Y							*Do fast loop which scans across white space a word at a time:ImPr_white_loop				lda [ParamLongD],y					;get a word-full of source pixels							cmp #$FFFF							;compare for all-std-white pixels							bne ImPr_not_white					;go mark the pr buffer if not whiteImPr_white_next				inc ParamWordF						;increment index into pr pix buffer							iny									;increment for getting next src word							inyImPr_white_eoln				cpy #$0000							;NOTE: operand is stuffed							bcc ImPr_white_loop					;loop until out of bytes in src line							bra ImPr_done_converting			;branch if done with all bytes*A source pixel word containing at least one non-white pixel has been encountered:ImPr_not_white*Convert word-full of source pix in ACC to a byte-full of printer pix and store in pr-pix-buffer:							phy									;save 16-bit Y which has src h index							sep #$20+$10						;set shortm+shortx: 8 bit mem/A/X/Y							tax									;left src byte in A, right in B							lda SourceToPrintPixLookup,x		;lo src byte -> 4 bits of pr pixels							asl a								;shift into position; lo src byte's							asl a								;pr pix nibble will be the high							asl a								;nibble of the pr pix byte that we're							asl a								;currently forming							sta ParamWordA						;this will become lo nibble of pr pix							xba									;now get high (right) source byte							tax									;get 8 bits of source pixels in X							lda SourceToPrintPixLookup,x		;hi src byte -> 4 bits of pr pixels							ora ParamWordA						;bring in low nibble already obtained							rep #$10							;longx; back to 16-bit for buff index							ldx ParamWordF						;get current index into line buffer							sta PrintPixBuffer,x				;store 8 bits of print pixels							rep #$20							;longm; now everything back to 16-bit							ply									;restore 16-bit Y with src h index							bra	ImPr_white_next					;inc/loop back to white or this again*Done with converting a single raster.  We now have a full line of printer-ready pixels:ImPr_done_converting*Compress and send data to printer:							lda VerticalCondenseFlag			;send pr-line-buff data as compacted							bne ImPr_vert_1X					;if vertical condense is on, thenImPr_vert_2X				jsr CompressSend					;every single src line prints as oneImPr_vert_1X				jsr CompressSend					;line, else, prints as two pr lines*Periodically run idleproc and also see if the user wants to abort the printing process:							lda ParamWordE						;use vertical counter and mask off							and #ImagerIPAFrequencyMask			;with all 1's so that we get all-0							bne ImPr_done_iproc_exec			;periodically (ie, every 64 lines)							jsr IdleProcAbortCheck				;do iproc/monitor/cmd-period activityImPr_done_iproc_exec*If the abort flag is set, for any reason, abort at this time:							lda AbortFlag							bne ImPr_exit							*Increment vertical counters and loop back:							clc									;add the byte-width of the source							lda ParamLongD+0					;bitmap to our current pointer, so							adc SourceByteWidth					;as to point it to the next line							sta ParamLongD+0							lda ParamLongD+2							adc #0							sta ParamLongD+2														inc ParamWordE						;increment vertical counter							lda ParamWordE						;compare against last value							cmp SourceYLineEnd					;loop if not done							bcc ImPr_vertical_loop*Exclusive exit point; terminate graphics mode and exit with status in ACC/carry:ImPr_exit					lda #ImPrGraphicsFinishCommand							jsr WriteShort							lda AbortFlag							cmp #1							rts*Graphics mode commands sent to printer:ImPrGraphicsStartCommand	dc.b 5								;start raster graphics							dc.b $1B,$2A,$72,$30,$41							ImPrGraphicsFinishCommand	dc.b 4								;end raster graphics							dc.b $1B,$2A,$72,$42							ImPrGraphicsCompactCommand	dc.b 5								;select data compress mode 2							dc.b $1B,$2A,$62,$32,$4D							ImPrGraphics75DPICommand	dc.b 6								;select 75 dpi size							dc.b $1B,$2A,$74,$37,$35,$52							ImPrGraphics150DPICommand	dc.b 7								;select 150 dpi size							dc.b $1B,$2A,$74,$31,$35,$30,$52							ImPrGraphics300DPICommand	dc.b 7								;select 300 dpi size							dc.b $1B,$2A,$74,$33,$30,$30,$52**COMPRESSSEND: Sends data in the print-pix-buffer to port driver (printer) in compacted format:**This routine analyzes the data in the PrintPixBuffer and then writes into the CompressPixBuffer*a compressed version of the data, according to the format of compacted-mode-2.  The total length*of the data sequence is inserted into a raster-transfer command sequence, and then this command*sequence, followed by the compressed data, is output to the port driver with a single write call.*Two subroutines, COMPRESSSENDADDDATANOR and COMPRESSSENDADDDATARLE, are used by this routine.*They add a discrete-data-block or a repeating-data-block to the output CompressPixBuffer; if these*routines are asked to add a block that is greater than the maximum-allowed length, then they*fullfill the request by adding several smaller such blocks.*CompressSend				stz cs_curr_pos						;init logical positions for scan:							stz cs_nor_start					;normal-run start and end, repeat-							stz cs_nor_end						;run start, repeat counter, and							stz cs_rle_start					;state: 0=normal, 1=maybe rle,							stz cs_curr_stat					;2=definetely rle; init for counting							stz cs_rept_ctr						;the length of the entire compressed							stz cs_outbuff_pos					;output ready for sending														lda PrintPixBuffer+0				;init "last group" to be always							ina									;different from first group							sta cs_last_group+0														ldx Resolution						;make sure we know when to stop							beq cs_res75						;scanning pr pix buffer, whose used							dex									;length depends on resolution setting							beq cs_res150cs_res300					lda	#300							;300 dpi * 8" / 8 dots/byte = 300							bra cs_res_setcs_res150					lda #150							;150 dpi * 8" / 8 dots/byte = 150							bra cs_res_setcs_res75					lda #75								;75  dpi * 8" / 8 dots/byte = 75cs_res_set					sta cs_end_pos		   cs_test						ldy cs_curr_pos						;head of scanning loop							shortm								;cmp current byte against last byte							lda PrintPixBuffer,y							cmp cs_last_group							longm							bne cs_diff		   cs_same						lda cs_curr_stat					;curr byte is == to byte last time,							cmp #2								;so dispatch to sameness handlers							beq cs_next							;if state=2, do nothing							cmp #1								;if state=1, go to its handler							bne cs_same_0						;else, if state=0, go to its handler		   cs_same_1					inc cs_rept_ctr						;inc rept cnt; if < thresh, continue							lda cs_rept_ctr						;repeat counter can make us go from							cmp #ImagerRLEThreshold-2			;state 1 to state 2 if >= thresh							bcc cs_next							lda #2								;we have beginning of a run, so							sta cs_curr_stat					;go to state 2 and do normal output							ldx cs_nor_start					;do normal add-data from nor_start							ldy cs_nor_end						;to nor_end-1 and then continue scan							jsr CompressSendAddDataNor							bra cs_next		   cs_same_0					lda #1								;same as last time and in state 0, so							sta cs_curr_stat					;go to state 1, clr repeat ctr, set							stz cs_rept_ctr						;possible repeat-run start position							lda cs_curr_pos							dea							sta cs_rle_start							bra cs_next		   cs_diff						lda cs_curr_stat					;curr byte not == to byte last time,							bne cs_diff_12						;so go to non-equal state handlers		   cs_diff_0					lda cs_curr_pos						;different and in state 0: state							sta cs_nor_end						;stays 0, and track nor_end with							bra cs_next							;curr_pos and continue scan		   cs_diff_12					cmp #1							bne cs_diff_2		   cs_diff_1					stz cs_curr_stat					;diff and in state 1: state goes							stz cs_rept_ctr						;to 0, clear repeat counter,							lda cs_curr_pos						;and track nor_end with							sta cs_nor_end						;curr_pos and continue scan							bra cs_next		   cs_diff_2					stz cs_curr_stat					;diff and in state 2: state goes							lda cs_curr_pos						;to 0, reset normal start/end,							sta cs_nor_start					;do run-length output							sta cs_nor_end							ldx cs_rle_start					;do rle output from rle_start							ldy cs_curr_pos						;to curr_pos-1, and then							jsr CompressSendAddDataRle			;drop thru to cs_nextcs_next						ldy cs_curr_pos						;next position: set last_group,							shortm								;increment pos, see if done							lda PrintPixBuffer,y				;copy 1 byte from pr pix buffer							sta cs_last_group					;so we can compare to next one							longm		   cs_next_inc					inc cs_curr_pos						;increment current position,							lda cs_curr_pos						;loop until out of bytes used							cmp cs_end_pos						;in pr pix buff for current							bcs cs_flush						;resolution setting							brl cs_test							;go to top of loop or to end-flushcs_flush					lda cs_curr_stat					;final flush: check state							cmp #2							beq cs_flush2		   cs_flush01					ldx cs_nor_start					;flush/state=0 or 1: do normal							ldy cs_curr_pos						;output from nor_start to curr_pos-1							jsr CompressSendAddDataNor			;and then go send output command							bra cs_send_cmdcs_flush2					ldx cs_rle_start					;flush/state=2: do rle output from							ldy cs_curr_pos						;rle_start to curr_pos-1							jsr CompressSendAddDataRle			;and drop into send-output-commandcs_send_cmd					pushword cs_outbuff_pos				;put length of data in cmd sequence							pushlong #CompressXferCmdLength		;pass where to put ascii number							pushword #4							;pass that it's 4 digits long							pushword #0							;pass that it's unsigned							_Int2Dec							cs_send_cmd_xmit			lda cs_outbuff_pos					;xmit bytes for entire cmd and exit							clc							adc #CompressXferCmdEnd-CompressXferCmdBegin							ldx #CompressXferCmdBegin							ldy #^CompressXferCmdBegin							brl WriteLong						;length in A, ptr in X and Y*Subroutine to add non-repeating graphics data to data in compress-pix-buffer (from->X, to->Y):CompressSendAddDataNor		stx cs_addbuff_from					;save the "from" pos in pr pix buff							dey									;save the "to"-1 pos in pr pix buff							sty cs_addbuff_to							tya									;compute ("to"-1) - "from"							sec							sbc cs_addbuff_from							cmp #$FFFF							;if this result is -1 then exit							beq cs_nor_exit							ina									;A now has number of bytes to do							sta cs_addbuff_num					;store itcs_nor_check_len			cmp #128							;cs_addbuff_num in A, check if not							bcc cs_nor_do_add					;too long: if ok, add it and exit														pha									;else save cs_addbuff_num total len							pushword cs_addbuff_to				;and save total "to" value							lda #127							;we'll do a chunk of 127 bytes							sta cs_addbuff_num							dea									;set chunk's "to":=127+total"from"-1							clc									;so that we're going from "from"							adc cs_addbuff_from					;to ("from" plus 127) bytes							sta cs_addbuff_to							jsr cs_nor_do_add					;go do a chunk of 127 bytes							lda cs_addbuff_to					;set "from" to our "to"+1, so that we							ina									;can continue next chunk where the							sta cs_addbuff_from					;one we just did left off							pullword cs_addbuff_to				;restore original total "to" value							pla									;restore total cs_addbuff_num length							sec									;we've done 127 bytes of it							sbc #127							;so subtract 127 and store and							sta cs_addbuff_num					;also leave the new value in A							bra cs_nor_check_len				;try again, with cs_addbuff_num in Acs_nor_do_add				shortm								;going to deal with 8-bit bytes							lda cs_addbuff_num					;build the +0..+127 opcode in A							dea									;do len-1 because #bytes pr is len+1							ldy cs_addbuff_from					;get "from" pr pix buff pos in Y							ldx cs_outbuff_pos					;get current out-buff position in X							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;store the opcode byte in out-buff							inx									;and increment out-buff positioncs_nor_copy_loop			lda PrintPixBuffer,y				;get discrete data byte from pr pix							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;buff and store into out-buff							inx									;increment our out-buff posn in X							iny									;increment our pr pix buff posn							cpy cs_addbuff_to					;loop for all pr pix bytes to copy							bcc cs_nor_copy_loop				;up to and including the pr pix buff							beq cs_nor_copy_loop				;position given by the "to" value							stx cs_outbuff_pos					;update output-buff position var							longm								;done dealing with 8-bit bytescs_nor_exit					rts*Subroutine to add repeating graphics data to data in compress-pix-buffer (from->X, to->Y):CompressSendAddDataRle		stx cs_addbuff_from					;save the "from" pos in pr pix buff							dey									;save the "to"-1 pos in pr pix buff							sty cs_addbuff_to							tya									;compute ("to"-1) - "from"							sec							sbc cs_addbuff_from							beq cs_rle_exit						;if this result is 0 or -1 then exit							cmp #$FFFF							beq cs_rle_exit							ina									;A now has number of bytes to do							sta cs_addbuff_num					;store itcs_rle_check_len			cmp #128							;cs_addbuff_num in A, check if not							bcc cs_rle_do_add					;too long: if ok, add it and exit														pha									;else save cs_addbuff_num total len							pushword cs_addbuff_to				;and save total "to" value							lda #127							;we'll do a chunk of 127 bytes							sta cs_addbuff_num							dea									;set chunk's "to":=127+total"from"-1							clc									;so that we're going from "from"							adc cs_addbuff_from					;to ("from" plus 127) bytes							sta cs_addbuff_to							jsr cs_rle_do_add					;go do a chunk of 127 bytes							lda cs_addbuff_to					;set "from" to our "to"+1, so that we							ina									;can continue next chunk where the							sta cs_addbuff_from					;one we just did left off							pullword cs_addbuff_to				;restore original total "to" value							pla									;restore total cs_addbuff_num length							sec									;we've done 127 bytes of it							sbc #127							;so subtract 127 and store and							sta cs_addbuff_num					;also leave the new value in A							bra cs_rle_check_len				;try again, with cs_addbuff_num in Acs_rle_do_add				shortm								;going to deal with 8-bit bytes							lda #1								;build the -1..-127 opcode in A							sec									;do 1-length because #bytes actually							sbc cs_addbuff_num					;printed is (-1*length)+1							ldy cs_addbuff_from					;get "from" pr pix buff pos in Y							ldx cs_outbuff_pos					;get current out-buff position in X							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;store the opcode byte in out-buff							inx									;and increment out-buff position							lda PrintPixBuffer,y				;get the repeatable pr pix data byte							sta CompressPixBuffer,x				;and store it into out-buff							inx									;increment our out-buff posn in X							stx cs_outbuff_pos					;update output-buff position var							longm								;done dealing with 8-bit bytescs_rle_exit					rts*Variables needed by CompressSend and its subroutines:cs_curr_pos					dc.w 0								;current logical position in scancs_end_pos					dc.w 0								;ending posn (#bytes in pr pix buff)cs_curr_stat				dc.w 0								;state: 0=normal; 1=candidate; 2=rlecs_nor_start				dc.w 0								;logical posn of start of normal datacs_nor_end					dc.w 0								;logical posn of end of normal datacs_rle_start				dc.w 0								;logical posn of start of run for rlecs_rept_ctr					dc.w 0								;rept count for run-length candidatecs_last_group				dc.w 0								;value of previous prpix bytecs_outbuff_pos				dc.w 0								;total length of compressed datacs_addbuff_from				dc.w 0								;save "from" param, in add buff subrcs_addbuff_to				dc.w 0								;save "to" param, in add buff subrcs_addbuff_num				dc.w 0								;save "to-from+1", in add buff subr**BUILDPIXCONVERTTABLE: Inits default source-to-printer pixel conversion lookup table:**The table has a domain of 8 bits and a range of 4 bits (stored in 8-bit bytes).  The table*is designed to be accessed with 8 bits of source (screen) pixel data (2 or 4 pixels if 320/640),*and returns a nibble full of printer-ready pixels.  In 640 mode, 4 source pixels are mapped into*4 printer pixels.  In 320 mode, 2 source pixels are doubled and are also mapped into 4 printer*pixels.  Since we initialize the table for either mode at this time, the imaging loop itself*need only use this table and need not decide on the fly which mode is in effect.  Furthermore,*since all possible values of screen pixels in the positions in a byte are enumerated in the*table, it is possible to map non-black/white pixels into a dither pattern.  Two subroutines,*MAP640PIXEL and MAP320PIXEL, are employed to perform the actual mapping of a source pixel.  These*routines are passed the source pixel bits in A, must return printer pixel bits in A, must*preserve Y, and may use X as a dither counter.*BuildPixConvertTable		ldy #0								;Y has count, X used by map routinesbt_loop						lda SourceMode						;branch on 320/640 mode							beq bt_its320							bt_its640					tya									;get a possible byte full of src pix							jsr Map640Pixel						;rightmost src pix in b0,b1 -> pr b0							sta ParamWordA						;init, pwA will build pr pixels byte														tya									;convert 3rd source pix -> pr pix							lsr a								;source pix b2,b3 -> print pix b1							lsr a							jsr Map640Pixel							asl a							ora ParamWordA							sta ParamWordA														tya									;convert 2nd source pix -> pr pix							lsr a								;source pix b4,b5 -> print pix b2							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							jsr Map640Pixel							asl a							asl a							ora ParamWordA							sta ParamWordA														tya									;convert leftmost src pix -> pr pix							lsr a								;source pix b6,b7 -> print pix b3							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							jsr Map640Pixel							asl a							asl a							asl a							ora ParamWordA							bra bt_next							bt_its320					tya									;convert rightmost pix in byte							jsr Map320Pixel						;source b0-b3 -> print b0 and b1							sta ParamWordA														tya									;convert leftmost pix in byte							lsr a								;source b4-b7 -> print b2 and b3							lsr a							lsr a							lsr a							jsr Map320Pixel							asl a							asl a							ora ParamWordA							bt_next						shortm								;nibble-full of print pix in ACC							sta SourceToPrintPixLookup,y		;store into a table entry byte							longm							iny									;goto next possibility of src byte							cpy #256							;go create all possible values of							bne bt_loop							;source byte; when done, exit							rts*Subroutine to convert 640-mode pix in ACC b0-b1 -> one print pixel in b0; must preserve Y, uses X:Map640Pixel					and #%11							;look at a 640 chunky pix in lo bits							beq m6_its_black					;branch if source is pure black							cmp #%11							;compare for pure white							beq m6_its_white					;branch if source is pure white							inx									;else it's in between, so alternate							txa									;increment wild count, consider as							and #%1								;alternating black/white if even/odd							beq m6_its_blackm6_its_white				lda #%0								;white source pix -> no ink pr pix							rtsm6_its_black				lda #%1								;black source pix -> yes ink pr pix							rts*Subroutine to convert 320-mode pix in ACC b0-b3 -> two pr pixels in b0-b1; must preserve Y, uses X:Map320Pixel					pha									;look at a 320 chunky pix in lo bits							jsr Map640Pixel						;consider this 4-bit pixel as if							sta m3_temp							;it were two 640-mode pixels next to							pla									;each other; this will still produce							lsr a								;correct black/white response and							lsr a								;will automatically impose a halftone							jsr Map640Pixel						;pattern on those 4-bit values which							asl a								;have 2-bit sequences other than							ora m3_temp							;"00" or "11", and we also double the							rts									;horizontal size in the processm3_temp						dc.w 0**CLEARPRINTPIXBUFFER: Zeroes the printer-ready-pixel line buffer:*ClearPrintPixBuffer			ldx #(PrintPixBufferEnd-PrintPixBuffer)-2							lda #0cl_loop						sta PrintPixBuffer,x				;WARNING: the line buffer length							dex									;must be even for this loop to							dex									;terminate correctly!							bpl cl_loop							rts**IDLEPROCABORTCHECK: IdleProc caller/command-period/abort address assert check.  May set abort flag:*IdleProcAbortCheck			lda IdleProcPtr+0					;(1) call user's idle proc, if any							tax									;if NIL, didn't specify idleproc							ora IdleProcPtr+2					;else build JSL instruction							beq ia_done_iproc							stx ia_goto_user+1							lda IdleProcPtr+2							shortm							sta ia_goto_user+3							longm							phb									;save env, call user, restore							phdia_goto_user				jsl $FFFFFF							;NOTE: operand is stuffed							pld							plbia_done_iproc							lda AbortPollPtr+0					;(2) check user's abort address							tax									;if NIL, didn't specify abort adrs							ora AbortPollPtr+2					;else build LDA instruction							beq ia_done_abaddr							stx ia_poll_user+1							lda AbortPollPtr+2							shortm							sta ia_poll_user+3							longmia_poll_user				lda >$FFFFFF						;NOTE: operand is stuffed							bne ia_assert_abort					;if user flag nonzero, set our abortia_done_abaddr							pha									;(3) check for command-period press							pushword #$0008						;pass keyDownMask							pushlong #ia_eventrec				;pass event record							_GetNextEvent							pla							beq ia_done_event							lda ia_event_msg					;check event message for period							and #$00FF							cmp #'.'							bne ia_done_event							lda ia_event_mod					;check event modifiers for appleKey							and #$0100							beq ia_done_event				ia_assert_abort				lda #$0080							;assert the abort flag							sta AbortFlagia_done_event							rtsia_eventrec:ia_event_what				dc.w 0ia_event_msg				dc.l 0ia_event_when				dc.l 0ia_event_where				dc.l 0ia_event_mod				dc.w 0**WRITESHORT: Immediately outputs pstr (len byte + data).  Pass 16-bit pointer->ACC:*WriteShort					tax									;save address from being clobbered							pushlong #0							;pass NIL for completion routine							push1 #0							;pass hi byte of hi word of adrs							phb									;pass lo byte of hi word of adrs							inx									;point adrs to data beyond len byte							phx 								;pass lo word of address							dex									;restore adrs to point at len byte							lda |$0000,x						;obtain word with length byte							and #$00FF							;isolate the length byte							pha									;pass the length							ldx #$1E13							;_PrDevWrite							jsl $E10000							rts**WRITELONG: Immediately outputs data pointed to by lo->X, hi->Y, and of length->ACC:*WriteLong					pushlong #0							;pass NIL for completion routine							phy									;pass hi word of address							phx									;pass lo word of address							pha									;pass the length							ldx #$1E13							;_PrDevWrite							jsl $E10000							rts**GLOBAL DATA: Variables and data that may be kept across imager calls:*PaperType					dc.w 0								;0..3 if Ltr,Lgl,A4,Env paper sizeResolution					dc.w 0								;0/1/2 if 75/150/300 dpiVerticalCondenseFlag		dc.w 0								;0 if v 2x (~cond) scaling; 1 if 1xIdleProcPtr					dc.l 0								;ptr to user routine to call or NILAbortPollPtr				dc.l 0								;ptr to adrs to poll for abort or NILSourceMode					dc.w 0								;$00/$80 if 320/640 modeSourcePixPtr				dc.l 0								;pointer to source bitmapSourceByteWidth				dc.w 0								;# of horiz BYTES in a source lineSourceXByteBegin			dc.w 0								;source bitmap X start loop valueSourceXByteEnd				dc.w 0								;source bitmap X end loop valueSourceYLineBegin			dc.w 0								;source bitmap Y start loop valueSourceYLineEnd				dc.w 0								;source bitmap Y end loop valueAbortFlag					dc.w 0								;if nonzero causes our abort**DATA TABLES: Lookup tables and buffers needed during the imaging process:*SourceToPrintPixLookup		ds.b 256							;lookup table: source pix -> pr pixPrintPixBuffer				ds.b 300+8							;one raster of pr pix; MUST be even!PrintPixBufferEndCompressXferCmdBegin		dc.b $1B,$2A,$62					;command sequence and accompanyingCompressXferCmdLength		dc.b 'XXXX'							;data to print one raster ofCompressXferCmdTerm			dc.b $57							;compacted printer pixel data inCompressXferCmdEnd												;compacted mode 2 (run-length-coding)CompressPixBuffer			ds.b 600+8							endproc							end